A||||16||Homicidal||I'm sick of my Fiero!||||9||
Z||000000||Homicidal||03-14-2001||12:40 AM||||When I got the car, I loved it, and I still love it, just runs great for the most part!<P>But it's size it now just downright annoying.  I'm 19, and I need a bigger car.  I should have known better than to buy this car as my only car and have it as a daily driver.  It's just not practical for...........anything!  Tiny trunk, 2 seater, tiny trunk.........<P>I've decided to buy a new car, probably a Saturn.  I could trade my Fiero in for the down payment, but I can't bear to get rid of such a beautiful, fun, and enjoyable car like my Fiero, especially one I've invested so much effort and time into.<P>So I will save up for my down payment (starting now) and I plan to buy a 1998-2001 Saturn SL series.<P>Love the cars, reliable, good gas mileage, and plus, I've heard they are based on the Fiero space frame technology.<P>I will put the Fiero on blocks (not literally) and file for a non-drivers permit, and keep the car for a later project (can we say V-8?) and in case I ever need a backup car.<P>So, any advice for a new buyer for a car?||||reg||9
Z||000001||Standard||03-14-2001||12:59 AM||||I'm gonna be 20 in about 3 weeks, and I've only had Fiero's since I got my license 3 years ago.  Sure, it's been a little small sometimes but that's what friends are for  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Never really had a problem with the small trunk, either.  Plenty big for a few 24 packs  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>So long as you don't get rid of the Fiero, everything will be fine.  You'll kick yourself if you do.||||reg||1
Z||000002||ElricSI||03-14-2001||02:29 AM||||You want a bigger car, so you want to get a SATURN!?  This car has the smallest front passenger area I have ever seen.  Saturn may be a fine car, but it should not be the first choice of someone looking for a car with some space.<P>Them Fiero's sure are mighty impractical (especially if you have a passenger), but can anyone name a car with better legroom?<P>------------------<BR>Proud Owner of 85 GT||||reg||6
Z||000003||Homicidal||03-14-2001||03:51 AM||||There are a few reasons I am getting a Saturn:<P>a) Reliable<P>b) Experience (3 people I know own them, and all love them with no problems)<P>c) Looks, they are really sleek and I love them!<P>d) Cost!  $12,000 fully loaded for a 2001 is pretty nice!!!<P>e) ANYTHING is bigger than what I got now!||||reg||1
Z||000004||voyagerspe||03-14-2001||06:12 AM||||Get a truck<P>Really, A truck will solve all your problems<P>1. lots of "truck" space for your stuff<BR>2. It can tow your fiero around<BR>3. you can drive the truck when you need space for stuff and you fiero when you want to go for a "joy" ride.<P>dont get rid of the fiero you will hate yourself later<P>||||reg||7
Z||000005||stsmithgt||03-14-2001||10:17 AM||||I agree.  If room is the problem, then a truck would fit the ticket.  Extended cab maybe.  The versitility of a truck is unbeatable comparing it to a Saturn.  You all ready have a sporty car.  The price may be right on the Saturn and a fully loaded truck is pricey, but a trip down to the wrecking yard, lumber yard, camping, puddle jumping, fishing, a trip to the beach or lake(I hate sand in my car)ever smell a wet sheep skin seat cover?, and kids?  The first thing my brothers kids did is get candy all over my interior. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">  It didn't bother me when I owned a truck. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I plan on getting a truck once my GT quits bleeding my wallet.  Believe me,  borrowing a buddies truck gets OLD.   My opinion, what do I know?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">¢²||||reg||12
Z||000006||firstfiero||03-14-2001||10:28 AM||||     I have my fiero and a 2000 chevy blazer. the only time i drive that is when I have to...kids. good car,plenty of space but around 30 grand...||||reg||12
Z||000007||bHooper||03-14-2001||11:05 AM||||i have my Gt and my '98 Cherokee.  i only drive that every once in a blue moon.  mostly drive the GT, of course the Jeep is leased, and i have 3500 miles to spread out over 6 months!<P>my next car, will be a SE, and then next spring i will probably get something like a celica, or maybe, just maybe, a '65 t-bird convertible   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>advice, keep the fiero, and find you a nice used cherokee, or rodeo, or pasport.  they can do all the hauling you need.. for $10-12,000 you can get a nice jeep.<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000008||FieroGTGirl||03-14-2001||11:15 AM||||I agree, the Fiero does have times when it is not the most convenient car...Like when you have more than two people or you need to do some serious grocery shopping....Not to say that Coconut isn't good at packing the trunk but.... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>We bought a 2000 Grand Am GT....I LOVE IT!!!!Especially since the Fiero is out of commission right now...(Can't wait to get driving that car again...)  The trunk space has been GREAT!!!!!! <P>But I had considered the Saturn...Nice looking cars!  Good luck! <P><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroGTGirl_sig5.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||BN Boomer||03-14-2001||11:17 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ElricSI:<BR><B>Them Fiero's sure are mighty impractical (especially if you have a passenger), but can anyone name a car with better legroom?<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeah, sure, how about a Suburban? If you can afford to buy and operate one, probably the ultimate in room, flexibility and utility. I've found that the Fiero makes good third car for my family of 5. It's great for my 17 year old daughter to drive as shee doesn't have much stuff to haul around and we aren't too keen on her hauling all of her friends everywhere.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||1FST2M6||03-14-2001||11:48 AM||||I've got a 92 Saturn SC2 with a 2.1 liter (20k) headers, new struts, Eibach springs, tinted windows and Alpine CD. asking $4000. We were gunna trade it in for our most recent car.. but we thought we'd need it since it's larger than the Miata and the Fiero... but we realized.. it's just taking up space in the driveway... Dark blue on Tan 5spd, a/c. also available are a set of 16" Kosei K1s with Yokohama A520s 250-45-16. $800.  I'm in Atlanta.. and may deliver... <P>IT's STOOOPID fast... lays down 161hp and 138lbft. My Fiance bought the car with a bad 1.9 in it.. we messaged it and POOF.. Civic stomper...||||reg||1
Z||000011||DavidHenshaw||03-14-2001||03:18 PM||||Hey Homicidal, you don't even have a problem. What about all those people who only have a motorcycle. You don't know what inconvenience is until all you have is a motorcycle. Compared to that your Fiero trunk is a Grand Canyon. You're not using it for a taxi are you?<P>Dave <P>86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000012||Fformula88||03-14-2001||03:48 PM||||If you want tons of space, and don't want to surrender too much sportiness, get a sporty hatchback.  I absolutely love my Probe as a daily driver.  The back seat is cramped for passengers, but the hatch will swallow tons of stuff.  Put the back seat down and you can move furniture!  Plus they handle great and the GT's are fairly fast!  If not a Probe, the Mitsu Eclipse, Cougar, or Celica are also similar sized with good performance.<P>Whatever you do, DO NOT GET RID OF THAT FIERO.  You will find the space is handy when needed, but you'll never be as satisfied with how a bigger car drives compared to the Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Sevaan||03-14-2001||11:09 PM||||I'm 6'4" and I feel the Fiero has plenty of leg room for me. And any passengers I have feel the same.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Homicidal||03-15-2001||03:08 AM||||Sorry, everyone who gets in my car looks like a giant compared to the size of the car.  I don't want TONS of room, but I want a car that just has MORE than what I do.<P>I realize I am not taking a Taxi, and I am not taking what I have for granted in any way.  After all, I paid for the d@mn thing myself!  I just want a larger sized vehicle.<P>You must remember, I am 19, and while my friends drive, I would <I>a lot</I> to be able to drive more than 1 person around.  It helps when going out with a large group of friends when we need more than just one car (which occurs often).<P>Saturns are atractive because they are the perfect size to me.  They are roomy, but not oversized, and since I've driven a few of them from my other friends, I like their handeling too!<P>I am definately getting a Saturn, but now I must figure out the method on how.<P>Pre approved loan from bank?  Financing company?  Dealership financing?  What options?  Stick or Auto?  What year?  How many miles?  Power or manual interior?  Many questions, lots of time to answer.||||reg||1
Z||000015||WKDFIRO||03-15-2001||04:24 AM||||The first car that I bought with my own money was an 87 Fiero coupe when I was 20. After the accident I got an 85 GT and have been playing with it for the last 4 years now...<P>Only last year did I finally get a slightly bigger car, well okay a Pontiac Grand Prix is HUGE compared to a Fiero but at least I can drive other people in it. Fieros can go through life with a small trunk but it depends on the life you lead I suppose...<P>The only reason I didn't get a Saturn...ALL of my friends have Saturns and I hate being a part of the crowd! <P>And I still have the 85 GT.<p>[This message has been edited by WKDFIRO (edited 03-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000016||AusFiero||03-15-2001||10:53 PM||||On finance shopping for the best interest rate is your only option.<P>Buying a new car...well...reconsider. I have bought 2 new cars in my life out of 46 cars to date. Regretted it both times. <BR>Look around at auction houses, dealers or private for a 6 to 12 month old used version of the car you are after.<BR>You will save big bucks if you shop smart and the car will be as new anyway.<P>My last 4 cars (excluding my Fiero) have all been less than 12 months old when I purchased them and have had low mileage and still covered by new car warranties. Best bit I have ended up with better optioned cars for a fraction of the new cost.||||reg||1
